, hypertension, cardiac arrhythmias, seizures, and dementia are associated with lichenoid-like reactions.":[5],"For lesions that are suspected to be oral manifestations of autoimmune connective tissue disorders (eg, pemphigus, pemphigoid, lichen planus), biopsies should also include specimens for direct immunofluorescence.":[126],"There are important disparities in access to dental care, tooth loss, unfilled caries, periodontal diseases, and oral cancers among the poor, near poor, and racial and ethnic minorities.":[112],"The interdisciplinary team working together can ensure that the needs of the patient are addressed in a timely and thorough manner.":[54],"Premedication is often considered for patients with risk for endocarditis, autoimmune disease, chemotherapy, joint replacement, or heart murmurs.":[85],"Oral health care should ideally be practiced in the morning when the patient wakes up, after each meal, and at their hour of sleep.":[34],"TABLE 32-7 ■ TOP 10 ORAL HEALTH OUTCOMES IN LONG-TERM CARE In some cases, patients are not able to gain access to care at each of these points in a day due to the lack of available assistance.":[58],"Atkinson JC, Grisius M, Massey W. Salivary hypofunction and xerostomia: diagnosis and treatment. Dent Clin North Am. 2005;49(2):309–326.":[33,55,96,116],"Bernabé E, Sheiham A. Age, period and cohort trends in caries of permanent teeth in four developed countries. Am J Public Health. 2014;104(7):e115–e121.":[21,54,109],"Calabrese J, Friedman P, Rose L, Jones J. Using the GOHAI to Assess Oral Health Status of Frail Homebound Elders: Reliability, Sensitivity & Specificity. Special Care in Dentistry, October 1999.":[41,57,153],"Chalmers JM, Carter KD, Spencer AJ. Caries incidence and increments in community-living older adults with and without dementia. Gerodontology. 2002;19(2):80–94.":[35,56,127,142],"Dye BA, Li X, Beltrán-Aguilar ED. Selected oral health indicators in the United States, 2005–2008. NCHS Data Brief, No 96. Hyattsvil